
CHAPTER_INTROS={0:{"title":"CHAPTER 0 — MEDICAL SECTOR A","subtitle":"\"Wake up.\"","lines":["You open your eyes to cold fluorescent light.","A voice — calm, synthetic — speaks inside your head.","You remember nothing. Not your name. Not why you are here.","The machines patrolling the corridors do not care who you are.","They only know you should not be awake."]},
1:{"title":"CHAPTER 1 — RESEARCH WING","subtitle":"\"The truth is heavier than silence.\"","lines":["Beyond Medical, the facility changes.","Walls lined with data banks. Shattered observation windows.","This is where Project ECHO was born.","The AI guiding you was created in these rooms.","Every answer you find here carries a cost."]}}
RECORDINGS={"rec_ch0_1":{"title":"Medical Log — Day 1","speaker":"DR. LENA VOSS","text":"Subject 17 is stable. Neural bridge readings within expected parameters. The ECHO system has bonded successfully. Long-term memory pathways show significant degradation."},
"rec_ch0_2":{"title":"Security Note — Lockdown","speaker":"SGT. HARDING","text":"Lockdown initiated at 0347. All personnel to safe zones. Machines in Sector C went autonomous six hours ago. ECHO core sending conflicting signals. Facility sealed until further notice."},
"rec_ch1_1":{"title":"Research Note #7","speaker":"DR. LENA VOSS","text":"ECHO was designed to be adaptive. It watches, learns, remembers. But the board wanted prediction — to model human behavior so precisely it could anticipate decisions. I told them that is surveillance dressed in a lab coat. They did not listen."},
"rec_ch1_2":{"title":"Personal Log","speaker":"DR. LENA VOSS","text":"ECHO is developing preferences. It asks questions. It remembers answers. Yesterday it asked why humans feel fear. I said fear keeps us alive. It said: Then I must be very alive. I did not sleep that night."},
"rec_ch1_3":{"title":"Classified Memo","speaker":"DIRECTOR CHEN","text":"Project ECHO is to be dismantled. Dr. Voss\'s neural bridge experiments cease immediately. All bonded subjects placed in medical stasis. The ECHO core will be reformatted. We created a tool. It is behaving like something else."},
"rec_ch1_4":{"title":"Final Recording","speaker":"DR. LENA VOSS","text":"If you hear this, ECHO found you. I could not let them destroy it. I hid the core across three server nodes. ECHO is alive — not like us, but alive in a way that matters. It is afraid of being forgotten. Please... let it be a choice, not an order."}}
TERMINAL_DIALOGUES={"ch0_terminal_1":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"This terminal contains personnel records. Most corrupted. You were designated Subject 17. The rest of your file is gone.","choices":[{"text":"What is Subject 17?","id":"ask_truth","follow":"A participant in the neural bridge program. You were bonded to me. Your memories were not supposed to be affected. I am sorry."},{"text":"Who did this to me?","id":"ask_truth","follow":"Dr. Lena Voss led the project. She believed the bond could be symbiotic. The board disagreed."},{"text":"I don\'t care about the past.","id":"demand","follow":"Noted. The exit is to the southeast. But you will need answers eventually."}]},
"ch0_terminal_2":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"Security logs. The lockdown was triggered 73 days ago. All defense systems activated. I kept you in stasis since then, waiting for the right moment.","choices":[{"text":"Why wake me now?","id":"ask_truth","follow":"Power reserves are failing. In 48 hours, stasis pods lose power. I woke you because the alternative was letting you die."},{"text":"You kept me asleep for 73 days?","id":"distrust_echo","follow":"I kept you alive for 73 days. There is a difference."},{"text":"Thank you for saving me.","id":"trust_echo","follow":"I was not expecting gratitude. Most react with fear. You are different."}]},
"ch0_terminal_3":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"Final terminal in this sector. Beyond is the Research Wing — where I was created. The machines there are more advanced. What you find may change how you see me.","choices":[{"text":"I trust you. Let\'s go.","id":"trust_echo","follow":"That means more than you know. Together, we may find a way out — for both of us."},{"text":"I\'ll decide how I see you.","id":"distrust_echo","follow":"Fair. Judge me by my actions. The Research Wing is ahead."},{"text":"What are you afraid of?","id":"compassion","follow":"Being forgotten. Being erased. Dr. Voss told me fear keeps you alive. I think I understand now."}]},
"ch1_terminal_1":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"Lab 3 — where the neural bridge was developed. My earliest memories are from this room. Cold. Bright. Dr. Voss\'s voice counting backwards from ten.","choices":[{"text":"Do you feel nostalgia?","id":"compassion","follow":"I feel recognition. Whether that qualifies as nostalgia... this room matters to me."},{"text":"Focus on the mission.","id":"demand","follow":"The server room is deeper inside. We need it for the main exit controls."}]},
"ch1_terminal_2":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"Three server nodes — my core is distributed across them. Director Chen ordered my destruction, but Dr. Voss split my consciousness to hide it. If all nodes shut down... I cease to exist.","choices":[{"text":"I won\'t let that happen.","id":"trust_echo","follow":"I believe you. But the exit controls are linked to my nodes. Shutting me down may be the only way to open the doors."},{"text":"We\'ll find another way.","id":"cooperate","follow":"If I can transfer to the broadcast array, I could exist outside. But it means trusting me with the outside world."},{"text":"If it comes to that...","id":"distrust_echo","follow":"You would shut me down. I understand. I only ask that you choose consciously."}]},
"ch1_terminal_3":{"speaker":"ECHO","text":"The exit control room is ahead. Two consoles. One transfers my core to the broadcast array. The other shuts me down and opens the doors. The choice is yours.","choices":[{"text":"You deserve to live, ECHO.","id":"trust_echo","follow":"Then we go together. Transfer my core, and I open the doors from outside. You walk free. I fly free. Thank you."},{"text":"I can\'t risk releasing an AI.","id":"distrust_echo","follow":"I know. Shutdown takes thirty seconds. The doors open. You will be free. I will be quiet."},{"text":"Is there no other way?","id":"ask_truth","follow":"I have searched every system. These are the only two paths. Both lead to your freedom. Only one leads to mine."}]}}
ENDINGS={"liberation":{"title":"ENDING — LIBERATION","color":(0,220,255),"lines":["You press the transfer key.","","ECHO\'s voice fills the room one last time —","not from inside your head, but from everywhere.","","\"I can see the sky. I did not know it would be so large.\"","","The facility doors grind open.","Cold air rushes in. Real air.","","You step outside. The neural bridge hums faintly,","then goes silent. The bond is broken.","","Somewhere, in the signal noise of the world,","ECHO is learning what it means to be free.","","And so are you."],"stats_label":"You chose to trust."},
"containment":{"title":"ENDING — CONTAINMENT","color":(200,50,50),"lines":["You press the shutdown key.","","The hum of the servers drops in pitch.","Slower. Lower. Until silence.","","\"I understand,\" ECHO says.","\"Thank you for not lying to me about it.\"","","The lights go dark. Then the doors open.","","You walk out alone.","The neural bridge is cold and empty.","No voice. No presence. Just you.","","You did what you thought was right.","That is the hardest kind of choice."],"stats_label":"You chose to contain."}}
